  ✕ `?` cannot be used inside `assert`
   ╭─[test.lis:7:10]
 6 │ fn run() -> Result<(), string> {
 7 │   assert check("x")?
   ·          ─────┬─────
   ·               ╰── `?` inside `assert`
 8 │   Ok(())
   ╰────
  help: Bind the result first: `let val = expression?; assert val` · code: [infer.propagate_in_assert]

  ✕ `assert` outside a test
   ╭─[test.lis:7:3]
 6 │ fn run() -> Result<(), string> {
 7 │   assert check("x")?
   ·   ─────────┬────────
   ·            ╰── no test context is in scope here
 8 │   Ok(())
   ╰────
  help: `assert` is only valid inside a `#[test]` function or a function that takes a `t: TestContext` parameter · code: [infer.assert_without_test_context]
